; Each balancing group chooses its own inferred exchange-price direction.
; When its first posting has neither residual commodity, the fallback is
; the first commodity that entered that group's balance, including when
; zero amounts or a cancelled transfer delayed the first nonzero entry.
; These are the bracketed counterparts of xact-price-inference-fallback
; and xact-price-inference-zero-sums.  In the mixed transaction the real
; group chooses USD, while the bracketed group independently chooses ZAR.

2024/01/05 Bracketed exchange with a zero fee first
    [Budget:Fee]              0 CHF
    [Budget:GBP]            100 GBP
    [Budget:EUR]           -125 EUR

2024/01/06 Independent directions with interleaved postings
    [Budget:Fee]              0 CHF
    Assets:USD               10 USD
    [Budget:ZAR]              3 ZAR
    Assets:ZAR              -20 ZAR
    [Budget:USD]             -6 USD

2024/01/07 Bracketed exchange after only zero entries
    [Budget:Fee]              0 CHF
    [Budget:Fee:AUD]          0 AUD
    [Budget:SEK]           -125 SEK
    [Budget:AUD]            100 AUD

2024/01/08 Bracketed billing after a cancelled transfer
    [Budget:Time]             2h
    [Budget:Time:Correction]  -2h
    [Budget:Income]       -1500 CAD
    [Budget:Billable]        10h

test reg --empty --format "%(account):%(amount)\n"
Budget:Fee:0 CHF
Budget:GBP:100 GBP {1.25 EUR} [2024/01/05]
Budget:EUR:-125 EUR
Budget:Fee:0 CHF
Assets:USD:10 USD {2 ZAR} [2024/01/06]
Budget:ZAR:3 ZAR {2 USD} [2024/01/06]
Assets:ZAR:-20 ZAR
Budget:USD:-6 USD
Budget:Fee:0 CHF
Budget:Fee:AUD:0 AUD
Budget:SEK:-125 SEK {0.8 AUD} [2024/01/07]
Budget:AUD:100 AUD
Budget:Time:7200s
Budget:Time:Correction:-7200s
Budget:Income:-1500 CAD {24s} [2024/01/08]
Budget:Billable:36000s
end test
